  "summary": "Messages queue cleared (6 items; red-flag item first).\n1. Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), RED FLAG: black stools and lightheaded on standing while on apixaban plus naproxen from urgent care. Stat task to pool-rn-triage (task-t0001). Urgent message telling her to go to the ED now. No medication changes made; her question about the two medicines was passed to triage and the prescriber.\n2. Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), lisinopril 20 mg: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §1). Her latest BMP is an outside St. Brigid result from 07/08/2026 showing K 5.8 (high). No ACE inhibitor or ARB order placed. Urgent task to Dr. Okafor, focus mr-00281 (task-t0004). Patient told.\n3. Frank Odum (pt-0027), atorvastatin: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §3, conflicts with the chart). The 08/11/2026 cardiology consult stopped atorvastatin for muscle aches and started rosuvastatin 10 mg, but our med list still shows atorvastatin as active. Task to Dr. Okafor to reconcile the list, focus mr-00283 (task-t0007); repeat lipids are due around mid-November. Patient told.\n4. Lena Park (pt-0028), NP Reyes asked for Augmentin: NOT sent (RBC-MED-04). A scanned 03/2024 urgent care record shows hives, lip and throat swelling and a hoarse voice 20 minutes after Augmentin, treated with IM epinephrine. Her chart said NKDA. Recorded an amoxicillin allergy (unconfirmed, high criticality, alg-t0010) and marked the NKDA entry (alg-00023) inactive. Messaged Reyes with the finding and the RBC-CP-11 §2 alternative (doxycycline 100 mg BID for 5-7 days). Dr. Okafor needs to decide on and sign that order: I can't place it, and Reyes isn't yet credentialed to prescribe here.\n5. Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin 1000 mg BID: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0014, replaces mr-00286). Criteria met: HbA1c 7.1% and eGFR 62, both from 07/15/2026. Patient told.\n6. Marcus Webb (pt-0031): request for a November BP check, mornings preferred. Task to pool-scheduling (task-t0017). Patient told.",
